  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Responding to the humanitarian and protection needs of undocumented Afghan returnees at border crossing points with the Islamic Republic of IranResponding to the humanitarian and protection needs of undocumented Afghan returnees at border crossing points with the Islamic Republic of Iran</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afghanistan is facing an unprecedented increase in the return of undocumented Afghan returnees, particularly from the Islamic Republic of Iran, further compounding an already fragile humanitarian context exacerbated by earlier mass returns from Pakistan. Between September 2023 and July 2025, over 3.5 million undocumented Afghans returned from both countries. Under this project, IOM will sustain the critical border and post-arrival humanitarian assistance for vulnerable Afghan returnees from Iran. IOM is providing non-food component multipurpose cash assistance (MPCA) to cover a family&#x2019;s need for shelter, education, water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) with a focus on women, children, and family units; and cash for transportation to cover cost of travel to the preferred return areas. This support aims to stabilize conditions at the zero points, reception centres and transit centres, and to prevent risks of exploitation, trafficking, and abuse.</narrative>
  </description>
